      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-01-25_WidnesExaminer_art0036" n="art0036">
        <head>RUGBY FOOTBALL.</head>
        <p>RUGBY FOOTBALL.</p>
        <p>THE NORTHERN UNION.</p>
        <p>Results of Saturday's Matches. NORTHERN RUGBY LEAGUE.</p>
        <p>G. T. P. Hull Kingston 11. 1 2 8 Leeds 0 0 0 qiunslet, 3 4 18 Bramley 1 1 5 Hull . l2 8 Huddersfield .......... • ...... 'Swinton Dewsbury 1 3 11 Rochdale H. ... 0 1 3 Ilr"ghton Rang 1 2 8 Halifax Wakefield Trinity 1 3 11 Keighley Bradford North.... 2 4 16 York Oldham . 1 3 11 Widnes Helens ............ 4 6 26 Coventry *lig" alford *************** . 5 525 Runcorn '..,* 8 Batley .............. 1 - 9 0 1 3 _</p>
        <p>- NORTHERN RUGBY COMBINATION. # Hurtslet A............ 2 4 16 Waisefield T A 0 1 3 Broughton R. A ... 1 1 5 Halifax A 0 1 3 Huddersfield A ... 8 14 58 Hall A n, 0 0 Widnes A ... 16 Oldham A 0 0 0 Warrington ........ 1 414 Leigh Shamrock 0 0 0' Wigan A 52 Runcorn A Rochdale -- 14 Dewsbury A 0 0 11 'Leigh A ........... 19 Wigan Highfield 0 1 3 NORTHERN UNION CUR—Third Qualifying Round EMillom lland ............. 0 1 3 Hebden Bridge 0 0 0 ......... 8 L. 55 Dearliam United 0 0 0 ,Peraberton ....... 14 Abram Rangers 0 1 3 Ditton Ilse ...... 11 Leigh Rangers 0 0 0 'Barton ............... 61 Bradi'd &amp;Clayen 0 0 0 WIDNES PLAY OLDHAM TO A POINT. The Oldham people sustained a severe fright in this match, for Widnes retained a leal until two minutes from the end. It was as a result of a blunder by Lomas that the visiting forwards rushed over under the Posts and Lloyd scored, Taylor adding the goal. The Widnes forwards continued to play the kick and follow np game, and it earned them a second try from a cross kick by Reid,ll O'Gara scoring, and again Taylor kicked the goal. From this point, however, Oldham gradually wore down the defence. D B Davies, with a strong burst, sent Jardine over for lye points before the interval. Just before three- quarter time E Davies scored a good try, but the goal- kick failed, and Widnes fought bard to keep Oldham Out, being only beaten when the final whistle was almost due, Longworth scoring after the forwards had rushed the ball over from a scrummage just outside. .Result ;—Oldham 1 goal and 3 tries (11 points), Widnes 2 ,Roals and 2 tilts (10 points). Teams and officials : 'ldhaln—Lomas, back ; Holbrook, V Farnsworth, Davies prid Williams. three-quarter backs ; Wharton and, W Farnsworth, half backs; Ferguson, Forshaw, 'BlP,tb, Jardine, D B Davies and Longworth. forwaids. Widees—Brassington, back: Reid, Taylor, Dainteth</p>
        <p>and Laws, three-quarter backs ; Noon and J O'Gara, half backs; Aspey, Corcoran, Cosgrove, Higgins, Lloyd and H O'Gara, forwards. Referee, R H Jackson, St Helens. Touch judges, W S Chapman, Swinton, and A Johnson, Rochdale.</p>
      </div>
