        <p>U</p>
        <p>ience."</p>
        <p>Lodge Road, Southampton. ulsion is the best a•ticle of its ars' experience. It has always ;old or were run-down, and has iddy known, and I never miss (Signed) HY. SCOTT.</p>
        <p>'stage to the Road, London,</p>
        <p>one code of morals for men and another for women. He had oue religious messige, one code of duty for men and women. _</p>
        <p>"To the question 'Lord, when shall Thy kingdom come ?'an early Chrissian writer has preserved a reply which is said to have been made by our Lord Himself, and which is of singular interest in relation to the application of Christian principles to the question of Women's Suffrage. This is how it runs: ('he Lord made answer and said, " When the two shall have become one—And the outward as the inward —And the male as the female" Neither in de nor female i.e., when women shall have the same rights as men, then, and not till then, can the Kingdome come.</p>
        <p>E. L. B.</p>
