      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-01-25_WidnesExaminer_art0180" n="art0180">
        <head>LATE MR. S. HASSALL.</head>
        <p>THE LATE MR. S. HASSALL.</p>
        <p>Funeral at Grappenhall Church.</p>
        <p>In the old Churchyard at Graprenhall, the remains of the late Mr S Hassall, whose death, under pathetic circumstances, was recorded in our last issue, were laid to rest amidst many manifestations of sorrow and regret, on Saturday. The hi?ah esteem in which the deceased gentleman was held by all with whom he- came in contact, was evidenced by the large number of people from Warrington who followed the cortege. The late Mr Hassall was very prominent in musical circles, and a large number of representatives of the various choirs in the towns of Warrington and Runcorn attended to pay a last tribute of respect to one who was so popular The funeral service which was conducted by the Rector (the Rev H V Pigott, was charactei iced by quiet, hut none the less tcuching simplicity, there being 00 music whatever. The chief mourners were :—Mrs Hassall (widow), Mr and Mrs Hassan (parents). Mr and Mrs C Hassid' (brother and sister-in-law), Miss M Davies, Mr J Davies, Mr and Mrs Iludswell, Mr and Mrs G E Tilling, Mr and Mrs A Bennett, Mr and Mrs Birch. Mrs Hough, Mr and Mrs Hollowood, Mr N Hudswell, Mr McClimon, Mr J Hassall, Mr Butland and J S Tilling. As a business man Mr Hassall was exceedingly tell liked and at Hiphfield Tannety, Runcorn, he had endeared him-- self to all. As a consequence a large number—about 200— of the staff and employees, together with Mr R H Posnett, attended to ray their last tribute. Other. organisations represented were— Hiizhfield Male Voice Choir : Sixty members along with Mr John Leathwood (secretary), and Mr W Shaw (deputy conductor). Warrington Male Choral Union : A large number of members including, Mr W S Nesbitt (conductor), and Mr W Taylor (secretary). Warrington Musical Society : Messrs F H Crossley (conductor), W H Payton, Mus. Bac. (organist), G H Smith, W Lee, F Fieldhouse and C II Hoult. Warrington Cycling Club : Messrs G Anderton (captain), J Poole (sub-captain), P Bailey, C Berry, T P Throssell, F Garnett, F Fieldhouse, W H Bellian,. C E Houghton, C Spinks,W Whittle, J Hoult, G Finch, P Heywood, W A Ashton and A Taylor. Workingmen's Mission, Bank Quay, was largely. represented by members.with Mr A Tilling (secretary). Bold-street Wesleyan Church Choir : A number of members and Mr F Hickman (organist and choir- master).</p>
        <p>St. Paul's Wesleyan Church, Runcorn, was also well represented. Others present included : Mr R M Butland (Union Tannery),Mr E Lunt (Fleming's Tannery), and Messrs E Howard, A Brooks, W Owen, and J Holt. There were numerous wreaths and floral tributes. including those from: 'Lu,' "with grateful memories of his love,"Father and NI other,"Mother and Mildred,' " Florrie and John," Mr and Mrs Hough. " Lizzie, George and family," "Agnes, Alf and family," 'Uncle and Aunt, Son and Martha," "Uncle John and Aunt Mary Ann," "Cousin Joe and Sarah Ann," "James and Jessie," "Alfred, Nellie and Fred," "Annie and Norman," "Mac and Mary," "Percy and Ade'aide," " Edie and Annie," Mr and Mrs Chas Smith and "Amy," (Runcorn) "Herbert Parkinson, Kingston- on-Thames," "Fred and George," "Percy," "Reg and Jessie," Mr and Mrs J Greenhalgh, Runcorn Mr and Mrs G Mackie, Runcorn; Mr and Mrs W P Baker, Wolverhampton; Mr and Mrs Walter S Nesbitt Mr B H Tilston,Mr and Mrs J E Hannan, Mr and Mrs Williamson, Mr and Mrs Levi Richardson, Mr R H Ashman, London; Annie Booth and Mrs Vanstone, Directors Highfield Tannery Co.. Office staff, ware- house staff and works foreman, Highfield ; employes Highfield Tannery Co., "Chums at camp," Manchester. Orpheus Glee Society, Warrington Male Choral Union, Highfield Choir, Warrington Musical Scciety, Bold-street Wesleyan Choir, St Paul's Wesleyan Church Choir, Runcorn; Working Men's Mission, Bank Quay; Warrington Cycling Club, Mr and Mrs A Brooks. The funeral arrangements were carried out by Mr H F Greenough.</p>
      </div>
